// checked the gold articles against the actual text on EUR-Lex (status: verified).
{"id":"q001","question":"Which AI practices are prohibited in the European Union?","lang":"en","type":"factual","gold_articles":["ai-act:5"],"gold_answer":"Article 5 lists the prohibited practices: manipulative techniques, exploitation of vulnerabilities, social scoring, predictive policing based on profiling, untargeted scraping of facial images, emotion recognition in the workplace and at school, biometric categorisation of sensitive attributes, and real-time remote biometric identification in public spaces for law enforcement, with narrow exceptions.","status":"draft"}
{"id":"q002","question":"Quelles sont les pratiques d'IA interdites par le règlement sur l'intelligence artificielle ?","lang":"fr","type":"cross-lingual","gold_articles":["ai-act:5"],"gold_answer":"L'article 5 énumère les pratiques interdites, notamment les techniques manipulatoires, l'exploitation des vulnérabilités, la notation sociale, la police prédictive, l'extraction non ciblée d'images faciales, la reconnaissance des émotions au travail et à l'école, la catégorisation biométrique d'attributs sensibles et l'identification biométrique à distance en temps réel dans les espaces publics à des fins répressives.","status":"draft"}
{"id":"q003","question":"What is the maximum administrative fine under the GDPR?","lang":"en","type":"factual","gold_articles":["gdpr:83"],"gold_answer":"20 000 000 EUR, or 4 % of the total worldwide annual turnover of the preceding financial year, whichever is higher, for the most serious infringements.","status":"draft"}
{"id":"q004","question":"Can a person ask for their personal data to be erased?","lang":"en","type":"factual","gold_articles":["gdpr:17"],"gold_answer":"Yes — the right to erasure ('right to be forgotten') under Article 17, subject to the exceptions listed in Article 17(3).","status":"draft"}
{"id":"q005","question":"Who may access data generated by a connected product under the Data Act?","lang":"en","type":"factual","gold_articles":["data-act:5"],"gold_answer":"The user of the connected product has the right to access the data generated by it, and to share those data with a third party of their choice.","status":"draft"}
{"id":"q006","question":"Que prévoit le RGPD en cas de violation de données personnelles ?","lang":"fr","type":"multi-article","gold_articles":["gdpr:33","gdpr:34"],"gold_answer":"Le responsable du traitement notifie la violation à l'autorité de contrôle dans les 72 heures (art. 33) et, lorsque le risque est élevé, informe les personnes concernées sans délai injustifié (art. 34).","status":"draft"}
{"id":"q007","question":"What does the AI Act say about cryptocurrency taxes?","lang":"en","type":"unanswerable","gold_articles":[],"gold_answer":null,"status":"draft","notes":"Not covered by any of the three texts; the system must refuse instead of guessing."}
{"id":"q008","question":"Quelles obligations s'appliquent aux fournisseurs de systèmes d'IA à haut risque ?","lang":"fr","type":"factual","gold_articles":["ai-act:16"],"gold_answer":"L'article 16 énumère les obligations des fournisseurs : respect des exigences de l'article 8, système de gestion de la qualité, documentation technique, conservation des journaux, évaluation de la conformité, déclaration UE de conformité, marquage CE et enregistrement.","status":"draft"}
